{
  "id": "separate-timedelta-serialization-mode-from-temporal-mode-in",
  "title": "Separate timedelta serialization mode from temporal mode in inference",
  "kind": "rule",
  "answers": [
    "Why does ser_json_timedelta change datetime or date serialization formatting in dump_json?",
    "How are ser_json_temporal and ser_json_timedelta resolved during inference serialization?",
    "Why are dates or datetimes serialized as numbers when ser_json_timedelta is configured?"
  ],
  "body": "Symptom: Configuring `ser_json_timedelta` unexpectedly alters the serialization format of all datetime, date, and time values during type inference.\nRoot cause: `pydantic-core/src/serializers/config.rs:SerializationConfig::from_config` fell back to assigning `TimedeltaMode` to `temporal_mode` when `ser_json_temporal` was unset, which `pydantic-core/src/serializers/infer.rs:infer_serialize_known` then applied to all temporal variants.\nFix pattern: Maintain distinct `temporal_mode` and `timedelta_mode` fields in `SerializationConfig`, resolve timedelta precedence via `pydantic-core/src/serializers/config.rs:TemporalMode::timedelta_from_config`, and dispatch `ObType::Timedelta` to `timedelta_mode`.\nConstraints: Applies when resolving deprecated type-specific serialization flags alongside broader group settings; does not apply to explicit type serializers that directly inspect their own configuration.",
  "applies": "Serialization configuration and inference for datetime and timedelta types in pydantic-core",
  "tags": [
    "serialization",
    "datetime",
    "timedelta",
    "inference",
    "config",
    "pydantic-core"
  ],
